  },
  "post_test_changes": "Only spaces around == in one matches! test guard after final strict; semantic tokens unchanged, then scoped rustfmt check passed. No production edit after final primary/related tests.",
  "acceptance": [
    "Same-origin aliases align by child position; independent bound named/selfjoin relation occurrences remain independent without payload equality.",
    "Element descriptors and Required text-policy identities survive reordering and aliases; bare projection is inert and provider activation remains consumer-owned.",
    "None, present empty and present NULL-child lists remain distinct; stored IEEE bits survive independent member expansion while scalar nonfinite use refuses.",
    "Inner eager selected projections and EOF precede outer expansion/filter/TOP; separate hidden atoms keep established membership semantics.",
    "Ordinary scalar/progressive APIs refuse retained-list plans before scans, including scalar-only final member output; typed API runs them without Source changes.",
    "One-MiB subprocess proof executes50 static named retained-list definitions and refuses51 before scans; existing mixed/named/joined absolute depth controls also pass.",
    "Every observed cancellation point, typed quotas, sticky visitor/source failure, retry, namespace ownership, external root registry and Count8KiB compatibility are covered."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No new list equality, grouping, aggregates, DISTINCT, UNION, streaming collection service, Core Value or Source API.",
    "Native Microsoft Access SQL alias-lineage, edge-result and provider equivalence qualification remains unrun; these are explicit TableCraft composition contracts.",
    "Typed execution remains cumulatively budgeted materialization; repeated whole-list copies and retained backing allocations are charged, not a constant-memory claim."
  ],
